# settlement-api: Repository Constitution

Owner: Settlement APIs. Change Owner: see CODEOWNERS.
Keep this file under 200 lines. Move detail to
.claude/rules/ (path-scoped) or .claude/skills/ (on demand).

## Source of truth
- Behavior lives in specs/settlement.spec.md.
- A ticket is a delta. If ticket and spec disagree, stop and
  ask for a spec change. Never infer a business rule.
- To ask, start your reply with a first line that begins
  `SPEC-QUESTION:` and stop. Hooks and CI read that line.
- Every behavior change cites its merged Spec Gate PR in the
  PR body as `Spec-Gate: #<number> <scenario IDs>`, or carries
  the no-behavior-change label. No approved delta, no code.

## Commands
- Install: `make deps`
- Unit tests: `make test`
- Contract tests (Gherkin): `make bdd`
- Lint and types: `make check`

## Architecture invariants
- Money is integer minor units. Never use float for amounts.
- Ledger postings are append-only. Corrections are new
  postings, never updates.
- Only src/settlement/fees/ computes fees.

## Working rules
- One task, one worktree, one PR.
- Never edit tests/contracts/ to make a test pass.
- Never read or print secrets, .env files, or credentials.

